@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam RoundCorner 8
skinparam ParticipantPadding 25
skinparam BoxPadding 15
skinparam maxMessageSize 235
skinparam DefaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam TitleFontSize 20
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #555555
    ArrowFontName SansSerif
    ArrowFontSize 11
    LifeLineBorderColor #BDC3C7
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #ECF0F1
    ParticipantBorderColor transparent
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #34495E
    ParticipantFontName SansSerif
    ParticipantFontSize 13
    ParticipantFontColor white
    BoxBorderColor transparent
    BoxFontName SansSerif
    BoxFontSize 11
    BoxFontColor #6F8592
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #FBC02D
    FontName SansSerif
    FontSize 11
    FontColor #424242
}

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowFontSize 12
    ParticipantFontSize 13
    BoxFontSize 12
    GroupFontSize 12
}
skinparam noteFontSize 12
skinparam maxMessageSize 270
hide footbox

title From one Pod to one observed workload\n<size:14>Direct reader mode | Illustrative acquisition</size>
caption Direct reader mode. Illustrative objects and counts; no live cluster execution.

box "Consumer process (owns client, mapper and lifecycle)" #EFF5FC
participant "Application\nconsumer code" as App #263D56
participant "Karta SDK\ndiscoverer + observation" as SDK #24638B
participant "Karta attribution\nlocal definition evaluation" as Rules #417770
participant "Injected reader\nclient-go adapter" as Reader #426381
end box
box "External service" #F1F3F5
participant "Kubernetes API\nobjects and Pod lists" as API #53616F
end box

legend left
  <color:#315E8C>Blue arrows</color>: calls / reads    <color:#39746B>Green arrows</color>: local decisions
  Dashed arrows: returned data    <color:#A54848>Red</color>: failure returns
endlegend

== A. Construct once ==
App -[#315E8C]> SDK: karta.NewDiscoverer(reader, options)
SDK -[#315E8C]> Rules: Compile catalog + exact-GVK overrides
Rules --> SDK: Validated, copied definition plans
SDK --> App: discoverer
note over App, Reader
  The caller wraps its dynamic client and RESTMapper with clientgo.NewReader.
  Construction performs no Kubernetes reads and starts no background work.
end note

== B. Find the starting object's workload ==
App -[#315E8C]> SDK: discoverer.WorkloadForPod(ctx, podRef)\nexample/training-0-pod, UID training-0-pod
SDK -[#315E8C]> Reader: Get Pod example/training-0-pod (UID training-0-pod)
Reader -[#315E8C]> API: GET Pod example/training-0-pod
API --> Reader: Pod, UID training-0-pod; controller Job training-0
Reader --> SDK: Detached Pod; requested UID verified
SDK -[#39746B]> SDK: Follow controller ownerReferences
SDK -[#315E8C]> Reader: Get Job example/training-0 (UID training-0)
Reader -[#315E8C]> API: GET Job example/training-0
API --> Reader: Job, UID training-0; controller JobSet training-set
Reader --> SDK: Detached Job; owner UID verified
SDK -[#315E8C]> Reader: Get JobSet example/training-set (UID jobset-uid)
Reader -[#315E8C]> API: GET JobSet example/training-set
API --> Reader: JobSet, UID jobset-uid; no controller owner
Reader --> SDK: Detached JobSet; owner UID verified
SDK -[#39746B]> SDK: Terminal root = JobSet example/training-set, UID jobset-uid
note over SDK, Reader
  Exact GVK mappings determine resource and namespace scope.
  Each edge checks identity, UID and scope; cycles, multiple controllers
  and excessive depth fail. Mapping calls are abbreviated here.
end note

== C. Acquire complete membership ==
SDK -[#315E8C]> Reader: ListPods(ctx, "example")
loop Every page, until continuation is empty
  Reader -[#315E8C]> API: LIST Pods in example; no label or phase filter
  API --> Reader: Pod page + resourceVersion + continuation
end
Reader --> SDK: Complete Pod list (illustration: 5 Pods)
note over SDK, API
  Scope comes from the terminal root. A cluster-scoped root requires all namespaces.
  Completed, terminating and unscheduled Pods remain in the list.
end note
loop Every listed Pod, including Pods outside this workload
  SDK -[#39746B]> SDK: TraceRoot: resolve its terminal controller
  loop Each required owner absent from this acquisition
    SDK -[#315E8C]> Reader: Get owner using its GVK, name, namespace and UID
    Reader -[#315E8C]> API: GET owner object
    API --> Reader: Owner object
    Reader --> SDK: Detached owner; requested UID verified
  end
  SDK -[#39746B]> SDK: Validate the full chain; reuse acquired owners
end
break Incomplete list, unreadable owner or invalid ownership
  SDK -[#A54848]-> App: nil, error (for example ErrIncompleteOwnership)
  note over App, SDK #FDE9E7
    Acquisition fails; no partial or false-empty workload is returned.
    A changed or missing starting object during collection also fails.
  end note
end
SDK -[#39746B]> SDK: Keep Pods whose terminal UID is jobset-uid; sort\nIllustration: 3 members, 2 unrelated Pods excluded

== D. Attach definition semantics ==
alt Exact root GVK has a Karta definition (this JobSet)
  SDK -[#315E8C]> Rules: Prepare declared instances from captured root
  Rules --> SDK: Instance IDs: "training", "evaluation"
  SDK -[#315E8C]> Rules: Evaluate each selected Pod's membership
  Rules --> SDK: Component, instance and replica coordinates; issues
  SDK -[#39746B]> SDK: Index membership for local scope queries
else Root GVK has no matching definition
  SDK -[#39746B]> SDK: Assign all members to generic component "pods"\nNo definition-derived semantics are inferred
end
SDK --> App: observed (*discovery.Workload), nil
note over App, Rules
  observed.Root() is the terminal root; observed.Pods() retains all confirmed members.
  Known kind: Definition() != nil, Generic() == false. Unknown kind: nil, true.
  This is a detached observation, not a cross-resource Kubernetes transaction.
end note

== E. Query the captured observation ==
App -[#315E8C]> SDK: observed.Pods()
SDK --> App: Deep copies of all 3 confirmed Pods
App -[#39746B]> App: CountPods(observed): total 3, running 3
note left of App
  Example fixture:
  training/0, training/1, evaluation/0.
end note
opt This JobSet example: Generic() == false
App -[#315E8C]> SDK: observed.Component("replicatedjob")
SDK --> App: component scope, nil
App -[#315E8C]> SDK: component.Instance("training")
SDK --> App: training scope, nil
App -[#315E8C]> SDK: training.Replica("0")
SDK --> App: first replica scope, nil
App -[#315E8C]> SDK: first.Pods()
alt Relevant membership is resolved
  SDK --> App: 1 Pod copy in training / replica 0\nA valid empty scope returns 0
else A Pod may belong but attribution is unresolved
  SDK -[#A54848]-> App: nil, ErrIncompleteAttribution
end
end
note over App, Rules
  A generic workload exposes its confirmed members through Component("pods").
  These queries perform no reader or API calls. Unknown component or instance,
  or a missing replica axis, returns an error. Outer scope bindings stay intact.
  Acquire again to refresh. Local karta.Workload edits do not change this observation.
end note

@enduml
